    "diet": {
      "word": "DIET",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Course of living or nourishment; what is eaten and drunk habitually; food; victuals; fare. \"No inconvenient diet.\" Milton.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A course of food selected with reference to a particular state of health; prescribed allowance of food; regimen prescribed. To fast like one that takes diet. Shak. Diet kitchen, a kitchen in which diet is prepared for invalids; a charitable establishment that provides proper food for the sick poor.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To cause to take food; to feed. [R.] Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To cause to eat and drink sparingly, or by prescribed rules; to regulate medicinally the food of. She diets him with fasting every day. Spenser.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To eat; to take one's meals. [Obs.] Let him . . . diet in such places, where there is good company of the nation, where he traveleth. Bacon.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To eat according to prescribed rules; to ear sparingly; as, the doctor says he must diet.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "A legislative or administrative assembly in Germany, Poland, and some other countries of Europe; a deliberative convention; a council; as, the Diet of Worms, held in 1521.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
